  "assets": [
    {
      "assetId": "math.func.function-notation/learning_objective/1",
      "kind": "learning_objective",
      "conceptId": "math.func.function-notation",
      "title": "Learning Objective",
      "content": "Given a function defined by a rule, the student reads and writes f(x) notation fluently — evaluating f(a) for a specific value, evaluating f(expression) by substitution, interpreting f(a)=b as \"input a gives output b,\" distinguishing f(x) (the function value) from f (the function itself), and using notation for piecewise, composed, and named functions.",
      "localKey": null,
      "language": "en",
      "refs": [],
      "span": {
        "file": "docs/curriculum/blueprints/math.func.function-notation.md",
        "startLine": 18,
        "endLine": 21
      }
    },
    {
      "assetId": "math.func.function-notation/misconception/MC-1",
      "kind": "misconception",
      "conceptId": "math.func.function-notation",
      "title": "f(x)-MEANS-f-TIMES-x",
      "content": "| MC-1 | f(x)-MEANS-f-TIMES-x | Student interprets f(x) as multiplication: f(x) = f × x; writes \"2f(3) = 2×f×3 = 6f\" or similar | Type 3 — language contamination (juxtaposition in algebra means multiplication: 2x = 2×x; students apply this to f(x)) |",
      "localKey": "MC-1",
      "language": "en",
      "refs": [
        "MC-1"
      ],
      "span": {
        "file": "docs/curriculum/blueprints/math.func.function-notation.md",
        "startLine": 28,
        "endLine": 28
      }
    },
    {
      "assetId": "math.func.function-notation/misconception/MC-2",
      "kind": "misconception",
      "conceptId": "math.func.function-notation",
      "title": "f(a+b)=f(a)+f(b)",
      "content": "| MC-2 | f(a+b)=f(a)+f(b) | Student assumes all functions are linear/additive: f(a+b)=f(a)+f(b) for any f; applies this even when f is quadratic, exponential, or absolute value | Type 1 — overgeneralization (linearity holds for f(x)=cx; students extend it to all functions) |",
      "localKey": "MC-2",
      "language": "en",
      "refs": [
        "MC-2"
      ],
      "span": {
        "file": "docs/curriculum/blueprints/math.func.function-notation.md",
        "startLine": 29,
        "endLine": 29
      }
    },
    {
      "assetId": "math.func.function-notation/misconception/MC-3",
      "kind": "misconception",
      "conceptId": "math.func.function-notation",
      "title": "f(a)-IS-f-APPLIED-AMBIGUOUSLY",
      "content": "| MC-3 | f(a)-IS-f-APPLIED-AMBIGUOUSLY | Student confuses f(a) = \"f evaluated at a\" with f · (a) (multiplication) or with f − a (subtraction); makes errors like computing g(x+h)−g(x) as g·(h)−g·x | Type 3 — language contamination (same notation as multiplication is extended inconsistently across algebraic operations) |",
      "localKey": "MC-3",
      "language": "en",
      "refs": [
